"text": "Now, why guess at all? Why not just say “I don't know”? The researchers argue that part of the answer is how models get graded.\n\nPicture a ten-question quiz. Right answer: one point. Wrong answer: zero. “I don't know”: also zero.\n\nTwo contestants. Both know six answers. The honest one leaves the other four blank. Six points.\n\nThe guesser takes a shot at all four. Four options each, so on average, one lands. Seven points.\n\nOne lucky guess. Three wrong answers. Somehow, a trophy.",
